Package: aucnull
Type: Package
Title: Heller Test of Equal AUCs for a New Marker in Nested Models
Version: 0.2.2
Authors@R: person("Satoshi", "Nakamura", email = "s-nakamura@med.mie-u.ac.jp", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Tests whether new markers improve the area under the receiver operating
    characteristic curve beyond established markers in nested models, using the maximum rank
    correlation estimator and the weighted chi-square null distribution of Heller, Seshan,
    Moskowitz and Gonen (2017) <doi:10.1093/biostatistics/kxw045>. The weights are estimated
    from the bootstrap covariance of the rank correlation estimate (or from a sandwich formula)
    and the curvature of the kernel smoothed area. The null hypothesis is that the best linear
    ordering of subjects does not use the new markers, and the test keeps its asymptotic level
    under any strictly increasing link. Clustered observations are handled by a cluster
    bootstrap. The likelihood ratio test, Wald tests with a robust covariance and the DeLong
    test are computed alongside for comparison.
